TAM-HIDE - WORKSTATION PRIVACY FOR TAMLINUX

tam-hide locks a Tamlinux workstation cleanly and without disclosing account
or session details.

Version 0.1.1 implements the Phase 1/1b Wayland session locker (`tam-hide`) for
use with `tam-pane` (0.2.0+) via `ext-session-lock-v1`, PAM authentication for
the current user, and idle output blanking/wake via `ext_idle_notifier_v1` and
`zwlr_output_power_manager_v1` (`--blank-after SECONDS`, default 30). Whole-seat
VT locking (`tam-hided` + `VT_LOCKSWITCH` + Argon2id multi-account selection) is
Phase 2; do not treat 0.1.1 as a whole-seat VT security boundary yet.

Follows the tam-idol 0.2.0 standard.

WHERE THINGS ARE

  src/        Wayland locker (tam-hide) and VT seat-controller prototype (tam-hided)
  tests/      unit tests and headless tam-pane integration test
  sandbox/    nested tam-pane demo for manual verification
  arch/       security and compositor design
  plans/      implementation phases
  work/       current handoff and session records
  ROADMAP.md  planned milestones
  UPSTREAM.md upstream code and references
